75a" :answer/id #uuid "9c024d47-b408-5e92-bcce-d5215b58421d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335372/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "9b6b16a4-d497-5b1a-b500-8e3ea9c495a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335372/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "99380087-c3bb-54f0-8397-985af8fdab73" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335372/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer-field/choices ["q-335372/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335372/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" "q-335372/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335372/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335372/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335372" :question/id #uuid "f2dd9dd4-da44-5101-8af9-d9e06c698ad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-335372" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{2}+3{x}^{3},$ then $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O({x}^{2}+3{x}^{3})$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,3{x}^{3}=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,{x}^{2}=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$  as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{{x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L3},$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand from line  $\\text{L4},$   we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and by $\\text{the transitive property},$  we conclude that\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335372/field-1" "q-335372/field-2" "q-335372/field-3" "q-335372/field-4" "q-335372/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
